Z||000018||IwannaIRM||10-09-2001||02:04 PM||||I still have my copy of that book.  I also have some original pics that they sent showing the different stages of construction of the stage I and I think one complete pic of the stage II.<P>Matter of fact I think I still have an original catalog from when Pegasus was in business back in the 80's.<P>------------------<BR>AIM - SWags2933<P>84 Fiero SE (being modified)<BR>88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000019||Slammed Fiero||10-09-2001||02:29 PM||||We have been talking about it on the Fiero racing list since it came out. <P>It's not a body kit for a Fiero , the IMSA street kits are loosley based on this design.<P>If you look at the decklid scoop , you will see it has a buldge at the bottom , a provision for an aircleaner. This was never used by any of the Big name teams that ran the car as it was outlawed by sanctioning bodies.<P>The car looks to be an original Huffaker / Dole / STP car. I have bits and pieces of info on these cars and from the pictures everything matches up. The decklid scoop is the big give away as to the cars originality.<P>One of our members on the racing list is bidding on it. I have no idea what he is going to do with the car, perhaps eligible for vintage racing soon?<P>There is a guy in the southwest who has one of these cars he runs for fun. It's a complete car with SD4 , used for weekend kicks.<P>A few years ago (10 or so) you could have bought a complete car for 10 grand with Sd4 , spares , trannies , just add driver. Problem is no one wanted them. Occasionally in the back of the SCCA magazine you will see a car turn up. The last one went for 16 grand a few years ago , it was a roller without motor.<P>Just on another note on the pic Oreif posted of the Kits the 2nd car belonged to archie in the early 90's or a customer of his. It ran NOS and a big stereo , I have the video from the early 90's that archie made and there are some nice drag shots of the car in it. I believe he wanted $9800 for the car.<P><BR>I want an ENTECH Fiero... Fun for weekend track events.<P>JM<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Oreif||10-09-2001||02:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by IwannaIRM:<BR><B>I still have my copy of that book.  I also have some original pics that they sent showing the different stages of construction of the stage I and I think one complete pic of the stage II.<P>Matter of fact I think I still have an original catalog from when Pegasus was in business back in the 80's.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Pegasus! That is the catalog that had the luggage, right? They had other accessories too.<P>Slammed Fiero, Archie Just sold the car again last year. He bought it back and added the hood vents then repainted it. I think he did some other work on it also. It doesn't have NOS now. Not sure if it had it before. Archie drove it around last summer until he sold it.||||reg||1
